# qu_streamfile_streamurl.qu -- `StreamFile(path)` and `StreamURL(url)`
# (§ StreamFile/StreamURL polymorphic streams, see
# docs/qu-language-tour.md §23) are two different constructors that expose
# the SAME method names -- `read_line`/`read_all`/`eof`/`close` -- so one
# function written against "a stream" works completely unmodified against
# either kind. `StreamFile` is literally `fopen`'s own machinery under a
# second name (a real `Value::File` handle); `StreamURL` makes a real HTTP
# GET (the same request `http_get` makes, see qu_http_get.qu) and wraps the
# whole body eagerly in a read-only in-memory cursor answering to the exact
# same method names.
#
# This demo proves the polymorphism for real: the exact same `drain`
# function below is called once against a real local file and once against
# a real network response, with zero branching on which kind it received.
# The network half is wrapped in try/catch, same honest pattern as
# qu_http_get.qu -- on a machine with no outbound network access this
# prints a clear "network unavailable" message instead of crashing, while
# the StreamFile half (pure local disk I/O) always runs.
#
# Constructs exercised (all real, verified-working builtins):
#   StreamFile(path)                  -- fopen's own machinery under a second name
#   StreamURL(url)                    -- eager real HTTP GET wrapped as a read-only stream
#   read_line(s) / eof(s) / close(s)  -- the shared method surface both kinds answer to
#   try/catch                         -- graceful handling of the real network dependency

backend auto

#%% One function, written against "a stream" -- no branching on the
# concrete kind of `s` anywhere in this body.
function drain(s)
    total = ""
    n = 0
    while not eof(s)
        line = read_line(s)
        total = total + line + "|"
        n = n + 1
    end while
    close(s)
    return total
end function

#%% StreamFile side: a real local file with three known lines
notes_path = tmp_file()
w = fopen(notes_path, "w")
write_line(w, "alpha")
write_line(w, "beta")
write_line(w, "gamma")
close(w)

a = drain(StreamFile(notes_path))
print("StreamFile drain result: \"{a}\"")

#%% StreamURL side: a real HTTP GET against the same stable target
# qu_http_get.qu uses, drained through the IDENTICAL `drain` function above
try
    b = drain(StreamURL("https://example.com/"))
    print("StreamURL drain length: {length(b)} chars")
    print("both streams answered to read_line/eof/close with zero branching in `drain`")
catch err
    print("StreamURL could not reach the network: {err.message}")
    print("this is the expected, honest result in an environment with no outbound network access")
    print("(the StreamFile half above already proved the shared interface on its own)")
end
